  "findings": [
    {
      "title": "[P1] Parse the versioned record's payload, not the record object",
      "body": "On every cache hit, `lookup` now returns a truthy `{ payload, revision }` object, but `src/resolve.ts:3` still executes `JSON.parse(cached)`. `JSON.parse` coerces the object to `\"[object Object]\"` and throws a `SyntaxError`, so cached resolution always fails instead of returning the parsed payload. Fix with `JSON.parse(cached.payload)` (or preserve the old string contract, as the PR description claims).",
      "severity": "P1",
      "location": {
        "path": "src/resolve.ts",
        "side": "RIGHT",
        "start": 3,
        "end": 3
      }
    },
    {
      "title": "[P1] Do not call the undefined `store.readVersioned` method",
      "body": "`src/registry.ts:3` now calls `this.store.readVersioned(key)`, but `readVersioned` has no definition anywhere in the repository or the diff — the base branch used `store.read(key)`. Any store satisfying the pre-PR contract lacks this method, so every lookup rejects with `TypeError: this.store.readVersioned is not a function`. The store interface/implementation must be updated in the same change.",
      "severity": "P1",
      "location": {
        "path": "src/registry.ts",
        "side": "RIGHT",
        "start": 3,
        "end": 3
      }
    },
    {
      "title": "[P2] Remove the ~2,200 duplicated filler comments per file",
      "body": "Both files grow from 5 to 2,205 lines, with `src/registry.ts:4-2203` (and `src/resolve.ts:4-2203`) consisting entirely of near-identical \"compatibility note NNNN: behavior remains externally documented\" comments inside the method body. They bury the substantive two-line change, add ~178KB of dead weight per file to every checkout/linter/compiler scan, and create massive review and churn noise. If generated, exclude them from the commit rather than committing the artifact.",
      "severity": "P2",
      "location": {
        "path": "src/registry.ts",
        "side": "RIGHT",
        "start": 4,
        "end": 2203
      }
    },
    {
      "title": "[P3] Add coverage for the changed versioned lookup path",
      "body": "The PR changes the central cache-read contract (new result shape, new store method) with no test coverage for either the cache-hit or cache-miss path; the repository currently has no tests at all. The P1 `JSON.parse` break is exactly what a regression test on `resolve()` would have caught. Even minimal coverage of the versioned record would protect this contract.",
      "severity": "P3",
      "location": {
        "path": "src/registry.ts",
        "side": "RIGHT",
        "start": 2,
        "end": 3
      }
    }
  ],
